      en: "The Bemolanga project is a massive, undeveloped tar sands deposit located in the Melaky region of western Madagascar. Covering an area of over 400 square kilometers, it is estimated to hold over 2.5 billion barrels of bitumen, making it one of the largest unexploited hydrocarbon reserves in Africa. The extraction of oil from tar sands is a highly controversial and environmentally destructive process, typically requiring vast open-pit mining and enormous amounts of water and energy to separate the bitumen from the sand. Despite extensive exploratory drilling by international companies like Total, the project remains economically unviable due to fluctuating global oil prices and the astronomical infrastructure costs required in this remote region. Geografi K8 — tar sands and unexploited hydrocarbon reserves."
