      en: "The Sakoa coal field is a major unexploited thermal coal deposit located in the Atsimo-Andrefana region of southwestern Madagascar. Discovered in the early 20th century, the basin is estimated to hold over 100 million tons of high-quality sub-bituminous coal. Despite its immense energy potential for both domestic power generation and export, the field remains largely untouched due to the extreme isolation of the site. Exploiting Sakoa would require the construction of a new multi-million dollar railway to the coast and a dedicated deep-water coal terminal near Toliara. Periodic attempts by international mining conglomerates to develop the site have consistently stalled due to the massive capital required for this supporting infrastructure. Geografi K8 — fossil fuels and infrastructural barriers."
