      en: "Fanalamanga is a massive state-owned forestry and timber processing enterprise based in Moramanga, encompassing roughly 70,000 hectares of pine plantations. Established in the 1970s, the company was tasked with managing the vast artificial forests of Pinus patula planted on the deforested hillsides of the Alaotra-Mangoro region. Fanalamanga operates extensive sawmills and processing plants, producing structural timber, utility poles, and raw materials for the national paper industry. The operation is a crucial component of Madagascar's domestic timber supply, actively reducing the logging pressure on the country's highly endangered natural rainforests. The company employs thousands of local workers in silviculture, logging, and milling operations. Geografi K7 — commercial forestry and timber processing."
