      en: "The Port of Maintirano is a small, essential maritime facility located on the remote western coast of the Melaky region. Lacking deep-water access, the port is primarily serviced by shallow-draft coastal vessels, known as boutres, which are vital for supplying the isolated district with basic consumer goods, fuel, and building materials. In turn, the port facilitates the export of regional agricultural products, notably dried fish, mangrove crabs, and beans, to larger hubs like Mahajanga. Maintirano is frequently cut off from the rest of Madagascar by land during the rainy season when dirt roads become impassable, rendering this small port a critical economic lifeline for the local population. Geografi K6 — isolated ports and coastal trading."
